@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-merge-assessment-uses-mobile-sheet
The optional merge assessment MUST be a separate section of the mobile review sheet,
using its plain heading and one card of rows, rather than appending an undifferentiated
list to the summary. Each category and verdict MUST read together above full-width
linked evidence. The assessment MUST NOT add nested cards, folding rows, numeric gauges
or decorative badges. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, rejecting the experimental UI and asking
for the app's design principles on mobile; DESIGN.md rules 49, 141, 171 and 172.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-review-shows-merge-assessment
A review with a merge assessment MUST, only after local experimental opt-in, show its low, medium or high level, all five
