@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-ai-code-cache-belongs-to-its-review
Private highlighted snippets and probes MUST be owned by the current review session,
source and head revision, and MUST NOT survive detachment or populate another review.
Requests MUST contain at most 400 lines and missing result rows MUST remain retryable.
A late result from an invalid owner MUST NOT refill the cache. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct
2026 shared session/source ownership plan and existing diff-highlight-respects-server-batches.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ai-code-reloads-for-the-current-view
A mounted snippet and pseudocode probe MUST reload for a new full view revision,
including a head A to B to A transition with unchanged final code and theme. Their
effects MUST stay stable while that view owner is unchanged. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct
2026 shared session/source ownership plan and the existing real Compose AI renderer.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] ai-work-looks-alive
AI work in progress is always a live, animated indicator, never a blank or a spinner. No
grey skeleton bars sit under it: Tavi called the bars under Ask's steps "awful" and took them
out, so the answer simply arrives where it goes (recording 15 Oct 15:37, 16:24 to 16:37;
L33; this replaces the hint bars of rule 71).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-thinking-line
While work runs there is one shimmering line, a present-tense verb and the elapsed seconds
("Working 12s"); when it ends the line becomes "Worked for 2m 3s" with a chevron that
opens the steps. The internal tool is never named (rules 18 and 72).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-steps-read-calmly
Each step is one plain sentence in regular weight after the icon of what it does, the
icon centred on its line of text. Only a failed step is red: a finished step ("Wrote the
answer") is never red, and no step ("Started") is greyer than the rest. One thing happens
at a time, and there is no "Wrote 3 of 6 stops, Active 3s ago, 4s elapsed" row
(rule 72; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 05:59 to 06:41; K13).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-no-machinery-on-content
A tour, a note or an answer does not show the model name, token counts or cache numbers,
and the work log does not start "Started Claude (model id)"; those live in Settings and
the model sheet. Rewrite is an icon at the card's corner with no word (rule 98; F58).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-links-look-alike
Links in AI text are teal text with no underline, all in one face: one cite is never in
the code font while the next is not. They sit on the text line and never grow it (rules
39 and 96; F40; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 07:36 to 07:44; K16).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-brief-rows-are-sentences
In the brief, a label and its value, and a finding's severity and its title, are one
paragraph that wraps as a sentence, never two columns where one wraps into a narrow one
(recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 19:49 to 20:16; N37).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design;security] shared-diagrams-use-inert-native-vectors
Both hosts MUST draw the same server Mermaid SVG as inert vector data, retaining its
viewBox, paths, fills, strokes, text and marker arrows. They MUST NOT execute SVG or
introduce a WebView. Inline diagrams MUST retain the existing natural size and fit;
full-screen diagrams MUST retain the existing bounded pinch/drag and close behavior.
Android MUST keep its AndroidSVG compatibility normalization and vector picture path.
Source: existing ai-brief-is-data and ai-structures-are-drawn, DESIGN.md rules 95 and
154, and Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 shared UI/native-adapter plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-diagram-results-belong-to-the-review
Private Mermaid source and SVG results MUST belong to one review session's current
source, key, head and view revision. Results from a retired view MUST NOT refill the
cache or display under a new view. Retained results and request coordination MUST be
bounded and completed or cancelled requests MUST release their coordination keys.
Cancellation MUST NOT become a cached failure. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026
shared session/source ownership plan and maximum-reuse native-adapter decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-ai-reading-requires-complete-results
The shared Brief MUST render every supported typed block, including code and Mermaid
diagrams, through the same kit and citation destinations. A read-only host MUST NOT
offer regeneration, paid setup or Analyze choices whose resulting passes it cannot
render. Standard and Deep MUST retain their existing Brief outcomes before those
choices become available. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse plan and
explicit requirement to prevent invisible paid work during the ordered extraction.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-analysis-adoption-belongs-to-the-view
Shared-analysis discovery and adoption MUST belong to the originating review source,
key, head and view revision. Late or cancelled results MUST NOT change another view's
saved work, reading mode, candidate chips or error. One adoption MUST run at a time;
a rejected adoption MUST keep its candidate and a visible recoverable error. Source:
Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 shared session/source ownership plan and existing shared
analysis chips, adoption and dismissal behavior.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ai-mentions-use-current-repository-paths
AI mentions MUST retain the existing repository-root path normalization and changed-file
whole-path/suffix lookup. Code names MUST use the existing unambiguous file-stem lookup;
private name indexes MUST live with their review session and current files, rather than
in a process-global cache. Source: existing ai-names-find-their-files and
ai-links-read-from-the-root, DESIGN.md rules 96 and 124, N17/N20, and Tavi's 21 Oct
2026 shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ask-thread-controls-keep-their-owner
Saved Ask threads MUST retain their original plain replies, live work logs, line labels,
follow-up input and close behavior on a capable host. A read-only host MUST NOT show
send, stop or close controls or issue their task/write RPCs. Sending and closing MUST
use the drawn session/source/head/revision; a retired callback or late response MUST
NOT start work, reload a newer view or publish its error there. A pending question MUST
be sent at most once and a failed start MUST remain retryable. Source: existing
ask-replies-are-plain, ask-send-needs-text, DESIGN.md rules 84 and 99, and Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 complete-result and shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ask-unsent-text-is-thread-owned
A saved Ask thread's unsent input and focus owner MUST remain stable during ordinary
recomposition of that same session, full view and thread. A different session/source,
head revision or thread MUST start with empty input and a new focus owner, including
a head A to B to A change which composition observes only at its end. Source: existing
AskComposer draft behavior and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ai-setup-reuses-the-persisted-model-and-complete-chain
Analyze and Tour setup MUST use the same source-owned model service as Settings and
show its persisted engine/model and supported effort before a launch. Choosing a model,
continuing a stale tour or dismissing setup MUST NOT start work. Every launch MUST check
the current host capabilities and retain all chosen passes, including Standard/Deep's
server-owned Brief chain and Deep's parallel critique. A retained control from another
source, full view revision or disposed setup MUST NOT start or queue work. Source:
existing ai-run-shows-real-model, ai-presets-start-the-run and tour-update-chooses-model,
and Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse and complete AI journey plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-analysis-launches-show-real-availability
Before the pull request has a current loaded view, Analyze presets and the custom
Analyze button MUST be visibly disabled and MUST NOT play pressed feedback, save a
new preset or announce a started run. Model and custom-pass editing MAY remain
available, and Generate tour MUST retain its existing explicit waiting interaction.
Once ready, one launch MUST start the selected complete analysis chain immediately;
a second launch while it runs MUST report the existing run without starting another.
Source: android-tappable-does-something, android-no-dead-ends, DESIGN.md rules53/63/82,
and Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse AI setup plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] shared-chat-keeps-the-original-conversation-and-history
Both hosts MUST use the original Chat transcript, reference attachment, streaming
answer, reader-owned scroll, source chips, copy/retry, starter questions and new-chat
controls. Earlier chats MUST use the existing searchable history and actual clear,
restore, saved-result and task RPCs. New chat MUST empty the drawn conversation in
the tap's frame, and a subsequent question MUST wait for that exact clear or restore.
Source: ask-replies-are-plain, ask-streams-and-cites, ask-scroll-is-the-readers,
ask-new-chat-is-instant, ask-history-of-chats and Tavi's 21 Oct maximum-reuse plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-chat-actions-and-drafts-belong-to-the-drawn-view
Chat input, pending questions and errors MUST belong to the exact session, source,
head and view revision. Reopening that view MAY retain a draft; a replacement view,
including an unobserved head A to B to A change, MUST clear it. A retained send,
retry, stop, clear, restore or source callback MUST check its current drawn owner and
latest host capabilities before acting. A question waiting for a local chat change
MUST NOT start after capability revocation or composer disposal and MUST remain
retryable while its view remains current. An old completion MUST NOT reload,
navigate, clear a draft or publish an error in a replacement view. A read-only host
MUST hide mutation and paid controls. Source: shared-ask-thread-controls-keep-their-owner,
client-invalidates-old-sources and Tavi's 21 Oct shared source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-analyze-is-one-action
Analyze changes MUST identify summary and file notes as its core outputs; its
preset/custom rows MUST identify extra tour, brief and review passes. Find problems
MUST identify findings (bugs, risks and nits) as its output; the two entry points MUST
NOT imply identical jobs. Tavi's 20 Oct 2026 feedback clarifying Analyze versus Review
with AI replaces the old unconditional three-output wording of rule 19.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;product] ai-review-sheet-is-plain
The AI review's findings sheet starts with "AI review (11)" in the sheets' one heading,
the count in parentheses, and folds nothing (rule 141). Bug, Risk and Nit are one
segmented pill, the kit's capsule, with All first; there is no Select all. The summary sits
in one white card and the findings are rows of one white card, never a box inside a box,
each with the Files sheet's check on its first line, and "Post N selected as a review"
posts the ticked ones ("no boxes inside boxes", recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 18:24 to 19:43,
N36, Tavi's decision).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] ai-launch-actions-have-no-selection
An analysis preset or review skill that starts work MUST be a button action with a
forward affordance and MUST NOT carry selected radio semantics or a selection tick.
General is not preselected merely because no review exists (Tavi's accompanying
20 Oct 2026 recording, 00:37 to 01:00).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-run-shows-real-model
Analyze changes and Find problems MUST show the persisted engine/model and supported
effort before any run can start, reusing the Tour model picker. Choosing a model MUST
persist it, return to setup, and MUST NOT start work; the subsequent request MUST use
that persisted selection. The menu tile and command MUST open setup rather than
immediately run. Look for problems on the Overview and a failed review's retry MUST
open that setup too. A retry MUST keep its previous review skill and the persisted
model/effort defaults and MUST require an explicit run action; findings and setup MUST
be pages of one sheet (Tavi's accompanying 20 Oct 2026 recording, 01:01 to 01:35, and
his consistency request applied to all manual run entry points).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-review-skills-belong-to-the-rpc-source
The cached-first review skill list MUST live in the active source's existing review
cache, without a process-global URL-only cache. Replacing endpoint, account or Access
MUST retire that list and any pending request. A late or cancelled reply MUST NOT
refill it or publish another source's error. Source: the accepted 21 Oct same-app iOS
source isolation plan and the original ReviewLenses server-owned policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-findings-publication-keeps-the-drawn-result
The same findings panel on both hosts MUST keep its severity filters, selected rows,
body, current-head publication and retry behavior. Posting MUST require current result
readiness, complete comment/review host readiness and server write permission, plus
the drawn result's variant, revision and head. A disposed, revoked or replaced full
view/result MUST NOT post or publish late selections, errors or review reloads into a
replacement. One publication MUST run at a time, and releasing an old request MUST
NOT clear another request's lock. Source: ai-review-sheet-is-plain and the accepted
21 Oct complete-result and source-owned iOS review plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-findings-confirmed-receipt-survives-sheet-dismissal
When a publication succeeds for the same current Session, full review revision and
result, its confirmed finding IDs MUST remain marked posted after the findings sheet
closes or host readiness is revoked. Reopening that result MUST NOT offer those IDs
for another post. Retaining this receipt MUST NOT change a closed reader's selection,
show its error or reload its reviews, and a replacement source, revision or result
MUST NOT receive it. Source: the original Android result-owned posted markers retained
by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision and the accepted source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-brief-rewrite-belongs-to-the-drawn-result
A retained Brief rewrite control MUST require the same current session, full view,
saved result and latest Brief capability which drew it. Removing the reader, changing
the source or result, or a head A to B to A transition MUST retire the old callback.
Both hosts MUST use the same explicit locale-bearing start action and MUST NOT start
a second Brief while one is running. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 complete AI
journey and shared source/view ownership plan, preserving DESIGN.md rule87's explicit
rewrite control.
